{"title":"Topicwise Test-22 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EC Electromagnetics-1","fileName":"079_Topicwise Test-22 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EC Electromagnetics-1.html","branch":"ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series Electronics Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n The Maxwell equation based on Ampere’s circuital law is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/e795dd4df40b5119c20228b5f06807ba8e26ecd2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/36033cec5cc1e58f49243693e49197ca4035cffb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/646aca30a9212481b10cf80f6093259bb86b3700.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/ed1cad654aea28e401b8afe45c3a12717a5b62e6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/e076b8a0e418931f6d0a41abd46db9a52d96985e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n A light beam is incident from air to a medium with a dielectric constant 4 and relative permeability 100. If the angle of incidence is 60°, the angle of transmission is ______ degrees<br />\n (correct to two decimal places)<br />\n  </p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"2.3","high":"2.6"},"solution":"<p>\n 2.48 (2.30 - 2.60)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/1e26d687265b5c1950c7b69f19adb8be3ee389f3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n A uniform plane wave with <img src=\"/media/8c0a0f9202be0244f991f1673d962a57811833d3.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> propagates in a lossless medium (∈<em><sub>r</sub></em> = 4, μ<em><sub>r</sub></em> = 1, σ = 0) in the +z direction. Assume that <img src=\"/media/9a05d82eec3b25e47f85adc82e607d481a105964.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is sinusoidal with a frequency 100 MHz and has a maximum value of 10<sup>–4</sup> (V/m) at t = 0 and <img src=\"/media/e29cf0fdc13a0af574177c6d986122b296592afd.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> The instantaneous expression for <em>H</em> is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/ec0c0ce472d44ec63eb9ae8e08868cabd6f886b9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/4c6b362a28f8faa9bef4f3e008d1aabf7f16239d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/569fd279b6d4f219cd39e32e6db58440dd9bc75a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/2bc0f5bdd56763cc311b673c1d04a7b6842329e2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/a1ed8fa00c609610ba33605c728998dab9c82ba3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n A sinusoidal electric intensity of amplitude 250 (V/m) and frequency 1 GHz exists in a lossy dielectric medium that has a relative permittivity of 2.5 and a loss tangent of 0.001. The average power dissipated in the medium per cubic meter is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n 8 W/m<sup>3</sup></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n 10 W/m<sup>3</sup></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n 7.2 W/m<sup>3</sup></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n 4.34 W/m<sup>3</sup></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/182b9727acb8a28b1310b2ce04b7fde012ac2c8f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":5,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,C","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Which of the following fields is/are genuine EM fields (i.e., they satisfy Maxwell’s equations)?<br />\n (Assume the medium is charge free, linear, homogeneous)</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/69372dd6eb867f7202ba068e80853dfba378cc7e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/03b135f30b108c0409eb294846fbcae56bb2bdd7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/0dbaf6c593c77cc3f10b1d9882674b17259c3c9d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/483833e018ca2ef3a16dbd542deb5237ceb02051.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a,c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/c19d905c8581cff3b8ee4371eeaa651491e3bb89.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/5480386dc4246616b601143111e24480f6d635a8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n </p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":6,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Which of the following statements is correct regarding the boundary conditions for electromagnetic fields?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n The tangential component of <img src=\"/media/74b06d8548ba1380f075936823840eb2bcccb0ab.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> field is continuous across an interface.</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n The normal component of <img src=\"/media/e365322e0a1c0273198aca3aadba2ec87e2ea9e8.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> field is discontinuous across an interface.</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n The tangential component of <img src=\"/media/d4ec13956e7c218caf04e8cf5eda54e033221d8d.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> field is continuous across an interface, where a surface current exists.</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/b08b281ce4504a56ec1be9bd899f84a74d1b12be.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n If 3cosωt – 4sinωt is expressed as <em>A</em><sub>1</sub>cos(ωt + θ<sub>1</sub>), then the value of θ<sub>1</sub> is _______ degree. (correct to one decimal place)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"52.5","high":"53.8"},"solution":"<p>\n 53.1 (52.5 - 53.8)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/5cdf19d665aa89409270deeb16ad071864be2694.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider <em>E</em>(<em>R</em>) of a TEM wave is given as <img src=\"/media/7a1642c6eec64bf6f397b49987f78912e739b088.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is a unit vector in the direction of propagation.</p>\n<p>\n A relation expressing <em>E</em>(<em>R</em>) in terms of <em>H</em>(<em>R</em>) is,  <img src=\"/media/3e1c01c16f1e02227c94f39a590c52bbeaf54fed.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Then the value of <em>A</em> is ___________ <img src=\"/media/41b6888ad27ddbd91d66392ba6ae5de6e0bc0900.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"-125","high":"-115"},"solution":"<p>\n -120 (-125 - -115)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/fdd24cd446dd6ab5e252af910c65677d0c681b28.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,C","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n The electric flux density is given as <img src=\"/media/301b41f84e7eaa96844a6fe65f52c3ee70ed2130.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> If ρ represent the volume charge density and <em>Q</em> represent the charge enclosed inside a cube of side 2 m centered at the origin with its sides along the coordinate axis, then which of the following options is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/72614618574a58a078ffffea9faf8cdb7548ecf8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/cbdeb4ac92f7c5af2929271b384656d9276fc3bc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>Q</em> = 8C</p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>Q</em> = 12C</p>\n</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a, c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/f20c33fefb467f8e3eac8ab5d8bd1d0549e9611d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n A volume charge density inside a hollow sphere centered at the origin with radius 2 m is ρ = 10<em>e</em><sup>–20r</sup> C/m<sup>3</sup>. The total charge enclosed within the sphere is ________ C (upto two decimal places).</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.02","high":"0.04"},"solution":"<p>\n 0.03 (0.02 - 0.04)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/8f7f6e70075266ab0af27384c622d5bdad8f24f2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n In a conducting medium, the magnetic field is given as <img src=\"/media/13c173d931a605de2a1f1f707129dc9640a55afa.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> The conduction current density at point (2, 0, –1) is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/6371f452b841889270ac557d374dd59cae1b5ea1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/1b135c283b45f9c80064550247624fda51abfc1c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/dee2bf748c8e43fe14b3973846fab06946e762f5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/d8438928ffa77b5fa07886ce22d818aedcf216fb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/aab7766e27a7b7c3f124187e787368efdacbdb61.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n A uniform plane wave at frequency of 300 MHz travels in vacuum along +y direction. The electric field of the wave at some instant is given a <img src=\"/media/e55ad99853ee3ef2587e0bdee0f04086533f6ea8.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> The magnitude of vector magnetic field at that instant in <img src=\"/media/b4a678ad99724013abbc0cecbe3df3628b579021.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> direction is _______. (correct to two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.2","high":"0.3"},"solution":"<p>\n 0.26 (0.20 - 0.30)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/a9139b67d78dbbde8652f4023639b7cd3ab32324.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n A square loop of 4 m side is placed in <img src=\"/media/8603ae1f958ce48919eadbf72876ab79ad327865.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> plane with its center at the origin and sides along the coordinate axes. If the magnetic flux density in the region is given by</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/a5ca8e255ee906a07801557a6b158827b8727306.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The emf induced in the loop at <em>t</em> = 10 sec is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 0.35 V</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 0.2354 V</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 0.92 V</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 0.61 V</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":