 of 8 and conductivity of <img src=\"/media/1b6b0e4a02cb8d6efe1489708b504359ef22b677.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> The average power density of wave at that location is _________ W/m2. (correct to two decimal places)<br />\n (Assume <em>f</em> = 300 MHz)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"6.8","high":"7.9"},"solution":"<p>\n 7.27 (6.80 - 7.90)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/d83257c360edfe736b1f9f2109af682cda2a1777.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":17,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n A material has σ = 0 and ∈<em><sub>r</sub></em> = 1. If the electric field intensity in the material is given by</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/a3818f2e391709d6bbf4d86edc2911a4e06e0de6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The value of μ<em><sub>r</sub></em> is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 3</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 6</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 9</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 2.25</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/8c85c66e0480261d85c94a394eba9fc262503131.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"}],"questionCount":17,"parsedAt":"2026-11-10T19:39:16.059Z"}